===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|kʷetwóres}}
From {{inh|en|enm|four}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fēower}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*feuwar}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from previous pre-[[w:Grimm's law|Grimm]] {{m|gem-pro|*petwṓr}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*kʷetwṓr}}, the neuter form of {{m|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}. {{dbt|en|cuatro|quatre}}.

Cognates include {{cog|sco|fower}}, {{cog|stq|fjauer}}, {{cog|fy|fjouwer}}, {{cog|nl|vier}}, {{cog|nds-de|veer}}, {{cog|de|vier}}, {{cog|nb|-}} and {{cog|da|fire}}, {{cog|sv|fyra}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂}} and, more distantly, {{cog|la|quattuor}} (whence {{cog|es|cuatro}}, {{cog|fr|quatre}}), {{cog|grc|τέσσαρες}}, {{cog|ga|ceathair}}, {{cog|hy|չորս}}, {{cog|lt|keturi}}, {{cog|sq|katër}}, {{cog|sa|चतुर्}}.

